Stepslider.mcc/Stepslider.mcc

   Stepslider.mcc is a Zune custom class derived from Numeric.mui. It is a
   horizontal slider over a few ordered steps, such as the compression levels
   of an archiver or the quality levels of a preview. A tick under the groove
   marks every step, so the user sees how many there are.

   The steps are the values from MUIA_Numeric_Min to MUIA_Numeric_Max. The
   knob only rests on a step: a click or a drag moves it to the step nearest
   to the pointer. The groove is filled from the Min end of the scale to the
   knob.

   Stepslider adds no class-specific public IDs. Numeric.mui owns the value,
   the range, the default value, the notifications, the cursor keys and the
   mouse wheel; Stepslider owns the drawing, the size and the mouse.

   The slider shows no text. The program shows the name of the chosen step
   beside it and updates it from a notification on MUIA_Numeric_Value:

      slider = StepsliderObject,
          MUIA_Numeric_Min, 0,
          MUIA_Numeric_Max, 3,
          MUIA_Numeric_Value, 2,
          MUIA_CycleChain, 1,
      End;

      DoMethod(slider, MUIM_Notify, MUIA_Numeric_Value, MUIV_EveryTime,
          app, 2, MUIM_Application_ReturnID, ID_LEVEL);

   Sizes follow the object's font: the knob is a little taller than a line of
   text. The height is fixed; the width is free, with a minimum that gives
   every step room for the knob, counted for at most 16 steps. Colours are
   the pens of the user's preferences.

   Ticks are drawn while they are at least three pixels apart. In a longer
   range only the two ends are marked; use Slider.mui for such a range.

   Header: <zune/stepslider.h>, which defines MUIC_Stepslider and
   StepsliderObject.


Stepslider.mcc/MUIA_Numeric_Value

   MUIA_Numeric_Value -- [ISG], LONG

   The chosen step. Numeric.mui clamps it to Min and Max. A change from the
   mouse, the keys, the wheel or the program triggers the ordinary
   notifications for MUIA_Numeric_Value. While the user drags, there is one
   notification for every step the knob reaches.


Stepslider.mcc/MUIA_Numeric_Min

   MUIA_Numeric_Min -- [ISG], LONG

   The value of the first step. Default 0.


Stepslider.mcc/MUIA_Numeric_Max

   MUIA_Numeric_Max -- [ISG], LONG

   The value of the last step. The slider has Max - Min + 1 steps. Default
   100, so set it. Changing the range of an open slider draws the new ticks
   and lays the group out again.


Stepslider.mcc/MUIA_Numeric_Default

   MUIA_Numeric_Default -- [ISG], LONG

   The step chosen by MUIM_Numeric_SetDefault and by Numeric's Toggle key.


Stepslider.mcc/MUIA_Numeric_Reverse

   MUIA_Numeric_Reverse -- [ISG], BOOL

   TRUE puts Min at the right end and Max at the left end. The filled part of
   the groove then starts at the right.
